{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/687141-what-is-the-main-talent-of-changelings-as-a-whole-besides-oneiromancy","id":687141,"title":"What is the main talent of changelings as a whole, besides oneiromancy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-03T09:21:02-07:00","id":687141,"title":"What is the main talent of changelings as a whole, besides oneiromancy?","content":"I believe they are good at watching each other's back, wording their promises just right and altering the senses/perceptions. However, the latter is mostly just the Mask and the Contracts doing their job. Would it be thematically fitting and mechanically feasible for changelings to have some illusory powers as inherent advantages of their template, like the Mage Sight of the Awakened and the shapeshifting of the Uratha? If yes, how would you do it? Turn some Universal Contracts like Mirror, Moon and Smoke into powers that can become more potent and/or finely tuned with more Glamour expenditure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T09:41:08-07:00","id":687188,"title":"","content":"I think if you wanted to pick one thing Changelings are naturally suited to (like vampires are suited to mind-control, werewolves to hunting, mages to investigation, demons to disguising themselves, etc.) it would be evading capture. Their powers help them run, hide, avoid notice, and escape captivity.<br /> <br /> We've seen a few spoilers related to this. One of the big benefits of joining a Court is gaining an Approach - a way to tempt those who would try to capture you into pursuing you on your own terms. I remember Dave saying he wanted 2e Changelings to be able to spend a point of Glamour to automatically escape binding or confinement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T14:59:27-07:00","id":687559,"title":"","content":"They got it, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T21:14:01-07:00","id":687892,"title":"","content":"I don't now a lot with anglo-saxon fairy tales, but in those I'm familiar with, fae almost all display the ability to go around unseen, predict or influence the future, create illusions, affect the health or integrity of living beings and objects. Those already are or could become inherent changeling powers.<br /> <br /> The Mask is a very strong but specific lllusion. Talecrafting is a limited way to affect present and future events. The contract of hearth is a very limited way to bless/curse people that could work as something all changelings could do to fit all the stories of curdled milk, tangled hair, broken tools and other such traditional fae punishments. 1e Changelings were kinda lacking in ranged offensive ability (this perhaps change with the new edition?); this could perhaps be implemented with something like the fabled elfshots as an inherent power with a ranged attack for bashing damage avaible to all Changeling, it'd be easy and far from overpowered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T02:11:36-07:00","id":689498,"title":"","content":"The Hedge and the ability to instantly enter said other world is also very much part of many fairy myths and the Changeling game. Fairies tend to literally live in the world next door, being there one moment and being gone the next.<br /> <br /> Note that Changelings with a high clarity also have the ability to sense odd things. It isn't particular precise, and is more something inherent to the game mechanics and the Changeling's struggle between reality and illusion. It is part of the game though and it has the occasional impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T08:32:31-07:00","id":689752,"title":"","content":"Put simply, changelings are really damn good at being tricksy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T10:05:48-07:00","id":689851,"title":"","content":"Pledges, and the ability to bind and twist people 's. fates. Whoever and whatever you are, careful what you say and promise in front of a changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T10:10:10-07:00","id":689854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/687141-what-is-the-main-talent-of-changelings-as-a-whole-besides-oneiromancy?p=687188#post687188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if you wanted to pick one thing Changelings are naturally suited to (like vampires are suited to mind-control, werewolves to hunting, mages to investigation, demons to disguising themselves, etc.) it would be evading capture. Their powers help them run, hide, avoid notice, and escape captivity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my view too. I'm really hoping that the Mask rivals Demons' Spoofing for power (with the obvious exception that if you're Ensorcelled or otherwise have the Sight you see right through).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T20:19:36-07:00","id":736652,"title":"","content":"Okay, I think I understand the gist of it. But what if the changeling was not forced into containment, but tricked into going there? Could he still use glamour to escape? Does this glamour fueled escape power apply to non-physical prisons, like the pocket dimension of a Mage's Space spell or the Solitary Confinement Exploit of a Demon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T01:27:13-07:00","id":737353,"title":"","content":"The Changeling still needs a door, or something like it, to get into the Hedge. So it is certainly possible to capture a Changeling. All you need is a room with all doors and windows locked and nothing with with a door-like frame can be constructed. Mind you, some changelings have additional powers that make short work of a door (or even manacles and ropes used to tie up the prisoner), so the kidnapper might need some other tricks for specific individuals. One thing that is always good is to use cold iron manacles. Fae magic does not work on cold iron items.<br /> <br /> As for tricked into imprisonment, it depends. If the Changeling gave an oath not to flee, the Changeling can still flee. The character just has to suffer the consequences of breaking the oath, and those consequences are part of the wording of the original oath. It could be the inability to use glamour for some time, but since it only triggers *after* breaking the oath it can still be used to open a door into the Hedge and get away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}